window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>From the <i>USA Today </i>best-selling authors Stasia Black and Lee Savino comes a story of love, loss, surrender, and rebirth told in three parts, now complete in this trilogy collection. Come get lost in the story of the beauty and the beast that pursues her. HEA is guaranteed. </p> <p><i>Beauty's Beast</i></p> <p>“I’m going to teach you, sweetness. How to give yourself fully to me.”</p> <p>Her chest rises and falls rapidly. But her gaze doesn’t leave mine. “I don’t know if I can do that.” </p> <p>“You don’t have to do a thing.” I can’t stop myself from reaching out and touching her hair. My hand is huge by her face. I grip one of her damp locks, swallowing it in my fist. “Just let go and be mine.” </p> <p>She'll pay her family's debt one way or another....</p> <p>Years ago Daphne's father stole from me, and it’s time for my revenge. I’ll steal her away to my modern castle. Lock her in my tower. Make her mine in every way. </p> <p>She's Beauty, and I'm the Beast. </p> <p><i>Beauty and the Thorns </i></p> <p>I never thought I’d see him again. My first love, back from the grave. My captor and tormentor. He holds my past, present, and future in his scarred hands. <i>He owns me.</i> No matter how far I run, my path leads me back to that lonely castle. Back into the arms of the beast. </p> <p><i>Beauty and the Rose </i></p> <p>They say the gods will accept no small sacrifice. To appease them, you must give your all. I’ve sacrificed everything. Lived through loss and learned to love. To take the beauty with the pain. The rose with the thorns. This love story isn’t perfect, but it’s ours. We’ll hold onto it forever. And hope our forever is longer than a day.</p>"; 
